  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "2ca0eb0d-89b8-409b-9ab8-e7d4a6034df7",
    "name": "Allotex Content Taxonomy API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Allotex Inc. is an ophthalmic biologics and device company; it runs no developer program and publishes no product API, no developer portal, no API reference and no SDKs. The only machine-readable, credential-free surface it exposes is the WordPress REST API that backs its corporate website at us.allotex.com, catalogued here.\n\nThis document is DERIVED by the API Evangelist enrichment pipeline from the route index Allotex publishes at https://us.allotex.com/wp-json/ — 270 routes across 20 namespaces — and every operation below was fetched live and confirmed to return data anonymously on 2026-08-06. Routes that returned 401/403 without credentials (/wp/v2/settings, /wp/v2/menu-items, /wp/v2/themes, /wp/v2/plugins, /wp/v2/block-patterns/patterns, /wp-abilities/v1/*, /mcp/mcp-adapter-default-server, /contact-form-7/v1/contact-forms) are deliberately NOT modelled.\n\nTwo things a consumer should know. First, unlike many Elementor-built sites, content.rendered IS populated on this site, so the full prose of all 16 corporate pages — About Us, Science, History, Conditions We Treat, Procedure, Refractive Surgeons, Medical Advisory Board, Our Team, Careers, Press, Conferences and Contact — is retrievable. Second, the posts collection is registered but empty: the Press page directs readers to Allotex's LinkedIn page for news, so there is no on-site article feed to consume.\n\nThis is not a product Allotex markets. It is the site's own content surface, and it carries no published SLA, versioning policy, deprecation policy, rate limits or support channel. The wp/v2 contract itself is defined upstream by WordPress.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Allotex Inc.",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
}